  "changes": [
    "Derived from @tanstack/query-core 5.105.0: QueryClient, the query and mutation caches and observers, retries, focus, online and timeout managers, hydration and streamed queries.",
    "Timers longer than 2^31 - 1 ms (about 24.8 days) run as a chain of timers in the default timeout provider. The platform treats such delays as 1 ms, so a gcTime of 30 days collected an unused query at once and a refetchInterval of 30 days refetched every millisecond.",
    "Declarations type a query's AbortSignal as the runtime's, with a structural fallback, and VoidFunction as () => void, so they compile without DOM or Node types.",
    "The legacy build and the TypeScript sources are not shipped: 2.1 MB unpacked instead of 4.7 MB."
  ],
  "implementation": {
    "kind": "upstream-fork",
    "replacementStatus": "independent implementation pending",
    "targetScope": "QueryClient cache, request deduplication, retries, invalidation, cache updates, query observation and mutation state."
  }
}
